---
description: Rails API conventions for the backend app
globs: backend/**/*.{rb,yml,erb}
alwaysApply: false
---

The app in `backend/` is the Rails API for Sokong. Read `context/product/concepts.md` before inventing a domain object. Module name is `Backend`. Local and test databases are SQLite. There is no web or mobile client in this repo yet.

Keep HTTP behavior in controllers thin. Put domain logic in models or plain objects under `backend/app/`. Cover HTTP behavior with integration tests.

When a Rails API is unclear, follow `source-driven-development` and cite the Rails guide or the API docs you checked. Do not guess framework behavior.

Record a contract change (path, verb, status, body) in the feature folder that caused it. Do not version the API until a second client exists. That decision is in `context/decisions/0003-start-with-a-rails-api.md`.

`config/master.key` and anything under `storage/` stay uncommitted. CORS stays closed until a real client origin is named.
